  "name": "The Illumination",
  "aka": [],
  "facts": [
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The Illumination was the Blinding Transformation of the year 994, in which the Eternal Light seized every human being of Moscavian bloodline and reshaped them into the Owl-folk, an event the Church of the Eternal Light interprets as the supreme act of divine revelation.",
      "since": 994,
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "Every human within the Tsardom of Moscavia—and across the known world—who could trace at least one grandparent to a Moscavian bloodline was caught in the Illumination's blinding light and transformed into an Owl-folk, while retaining their full human intelligence, memories, and personality.",
      "since": 994,
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The Illumination did not destroy the Tsardom of Moscavia; rather, the Owl-folk reorganized its governance, with the Tsar continuing to rule from a throne scaled to accommodate wingspans of eight feet or more.",
      "since": 994,
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The Church of the Eternal Light teaches that the Illumination was the Eternal Light's greatest act, raising Moscavia's children to a higher state of being.",
      "held_by": "Church of the Eternal Light"
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "Pure-line Moscavians—the descendants of four unbroken Moscavian grandparents—emerged from the Illumination as snowy owls, with entirely white plumage and smooth, pale faces, and they constitute the majority of the Tsardom's population.",
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "Eared owl-folk, resembling long-eared or great-eared owl species and exhibiting plumage ranging from tawny brown to grey to russet, arose among those whose Moscavian ancestry had been diluted through generations of intermarriage with non-Moscavian populations.",
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The Owl-folk transformation preserved each individual's human capacity for complex thought, language, and cultural expression, while instilling an innate preference for nocturnal activity and heightened sensitivity to sound and darkness.",
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The Illumination is commemorated as the defining event of the Church's theology, proving that the Eternal Light is the source of all creation and that darkness is the absence of divine knowledge.",
      "held_by": "Church of the Eternal Light"
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "Six years after the Illumination, in the year 1000, the transformed society of the Tsardom has adapted its architecture, legal codes, and daily rhythms to accommodate the Owl-folk, though the cultural memory of human form endures in stories, songs, and the faithful observance of Church rites.",
      "since": 1000,
      "held_by": null
    }
  ],
  "names": [
    {
      "name": "Tsardom of Moscavia",
      "kind": "place",
      "aka": []
    },
    {
