  "name": "The Illumination",
  "aka": [],
  "facts": [
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The Illumination was the blinding transformation of every human being of Moscavian bloodline that swept across the known world in the year 994, reshaping their bodies entirely into those of large owls while preserving their full human minds.",
      "since": "994",
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The Church of the Eternal Light interprets the Illumination as the Eternal Light's greatest act, raising Moscavia's children to a higher state of being.",
      "held_by": "Church of the Eternal Light"
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The transformation preserved each individual's full human intelligence, memories, and core personality, but reshaped their bodies entirely into those of large owls.",
      "since": "994",
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "Pure-line Moscavians—those with all four grandparents of unbroken Moscavian descent—emerged from the transformation as snowy owls, with pristine white plumage and pale, unmarked faces.",
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "Those whose Moscavian ancestry was diluted through generations of intermarriage with non-Moscavian populations became eared owls, resembling long-eared or great-eared owl species with varied plumage coloration.",
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The transformed Owl-folk retained their human capacity for complex thought, language, and cultural expression, but gained an innate preference for nocturnal activity and heightened sensitivity to sound and darkness.",
      "since": "994",
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The Illumination did not extinguish the Tsardom of Moscavia; rather, the Owl-folk reorganized its governance, with the Tsar continuing to rule from a throne scaled to wingspans of eight feet or more.",
      "since": "994",
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "Six years after the Illumination, in the year 1000, the Tsardom of Moscavia stands as a thriving northern kingdom governed by Owl-folk, its architecture gradually adapted to accommodate the changed population.",
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The Illumination is celebrated as a holy act within the Church of the Eternal Light and is considered the Eternal Light's ultimate revelation, transforming the faithful into beings of enhanced perception attuned to both light and dark.",
      "held_by": "Church of the Eternal Light"
    }
  ],
